      <p class="meta"><time datetime={pubDate}>Published September 14, 2026</time></p>

      <p>Good e-Reader published its “Top 10 Best e-Readers for Fall 2026” roundup this morning, and the list is unusually useful: two of the ten devices — the DuRoBo Krono and the Musnap Ocean — do not appear in any earlier 2026 buyer’s guide on our site, and several others have shifted enough since our spring coverage that it is worth re-mapping the category. Fall is also the first season in which the price-to-portability curve bends hard toward the pocketable end: every phone-sized or sub-7-inch model in the top ten lists native <strong>EPUB</strong> support out of the box, and three of them are explicitly marketed as reading-first rather than tablet-first.</p>

      <p>This guide walks through the roundup in order, adds an EPUB-centric column to each device (so you can see what you can read natively versus what needs a converter step), and finishes with a buying recommendation keyed to reader type. Sources are cited inline; the primary reference is Michael Kozlowski, <em>The Top 10 Best e-Readers for Fall 2026</em>, Good e-Reader, September 13–14 2026.</p>

